    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey can u help me understand this part of an nda i just got? it says: \"The Receiving Party shall indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the Disclosing Party from and against any and all losses, damages, liabilities, costs, and expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees) arising out of or resulting from any breach of this Agreement or any unauthorized use of the Confidential Information by the Receiving Party or its Representatives.\" basically what does this mean for me if i mess up?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sure! This is an indemnification clause, and it means that if you (or your employees/representatives) breach the NDA or misuse the confidential information, you'd have to cover all the costs the other party suffers as a result—plus their legal fees if they have to go to court. So \"messing up\" doesn't just mean apologizing; you'd be financially on the hook for making them whole.\n\nA few things to watch: \"Representatives\" likely extends your liability to your employees' or contractors' actions, and the clause language \"any and all losses\" is broad, so if you're concerned about the scope, it might be worth negotiating caps on liability or exclusions—ideally with input from a lawyer before signing.",
